sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Logic as Lua GameLogic
  participant Binding as SetUIValue binding
  participant State as LuaUIState
  participant RUI as ReactiveUI
  participant Parser as TemplateParser
  participant HTML as HTMLRendererMT
  participant Worker as Render thread / litehtml
  participant GL as Main thread / OpenGL

  Logic->>Binding: SetUIValue("data.gameStarted", true)
  Binding->>State: SetValue(path, value)
  State->>State: compare old/new; mark dirty if changed
  Logic->>Binding: RefreshUI()
  Binding->>RUI: GetRenderedHTML()
  alt state is dirty
    RUI->>Parser: Evaluate(state)
    Parser-->>RUI: complete evaluated HTML + handler map
    RUI->>State: ClearDirty()
  else state is clean
    RUI-->>RUI: reuse cached HTML
  end
  Binding->>HTML: UpdateHTML(cached HTML)
  HTML-->>Worker: signal pending HTML
  Worker->>Worker: create litehtml document, layout, rasterize
  Worker->>Worker: extract event bounds
  Worker-->>GL: swap front pixel/bounds buffers
  GL->>GL: upload changed buffer and composite overlay

  Note over RUI,Worker: “Reactive” means dirty-gated full template evaluation and full document render.
  Note over State,HTML: Frequent C++ FPS updates also call GetRenderedHTML/UpdateHTML from Game::TrackFPS.
